BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T180000
UID:69a5df971e64afd01e5f363d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect matches older adults with a teen volunteer t
 o provide tech help\, under the guidance of library staff. Learn the basic
 s of using tablets and phone\nand learn about topics such as\ntexting\, em
 ail\, and other communication devices\n. Get one on one support in a welco
 ming and friendly environment.\nPlease bring your personal device.\nIf you
 're a teen between the ages of 13-17 and would like to learn more about be
 coming a Seniors E-Connect volunteer\, visit the\nSeniors E-Connect Volunt
 eering page\nor contact the branch.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Yorkville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a5df971e64afd01e5f363d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 5: Use Windows
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T113000
UID:69d93d43f29b90618efdf8e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on essential basic Windows skills for absolute beginne
 rs with little computer experience.\nIn this fifth session you will:\nBeco
 me familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using common 
 Windows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, Applicatio
 ns\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic understanding
  of how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.\nPrerequi
 sites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and keyboarding skills\
 nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-
 5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d93d43f29b90618efdf8e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Life Skills for Seniors: Social Media for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T193000
UID:69de49484dacf581ff88aa24@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For people who have basic internet skills and want to learn ho
 w to get started on some of the most popular social media platforms. We te
 ach you how to create an account and set up your profile\, as well as unde
 rstand the different features and functionalities of each platform.\nWe'll
  also provide tips for staying safe and protecting your privacy online.\nR
 esource handout provided.\n*Registration is required\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de49484dacf581ff88aa24
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Social Prescribing and Healthy Aging: Improving Our Physical\, Cog
 nitive\, and Mental Health Through Connections
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T190000
UID:6a04a4d3c6a1dc3d00d37ab9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join journalist and author\, Julia Hotz\, in an exploration of
  how social connections improve the physical\, cognitive\, and mental heal
 th of older adults\, and the complementary role that social prescribing ca
 n have on health and wellness. Julia will showcase local and international
  innovative programs and frameworks facilitating connections for older adu
 lts – from dementia care farms and “wild” nursing homes to virtual p
 hone buddy programs and choirs. Julia will also discuss how social prescri
 bing can address issues such as emergency department overuse\, caregiver f
 atigue\, health inequalities\, transportation barriers\, and ageism\, and 
 share how community members can get involved in social prescribing and soc
 ial connection.\nJulia Hotz is a journalist and award-winning author of\nT
 he Connection Cure\n– the first book chronicling the science and stories
  of social prescribing.\nLight refreshments will be provided during the pr
 ogram.\nRegistration is required as space is limited.\nInformation Collect
 ion Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Second Floor\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a04a4d3c6a1dc3d00d37ab9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Evening Book Club & Play Reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:6972a805d2bbe265eb294671@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join other book lovers in your community and participate in li
 vely discussions of popular books.\nMeeting every 1\nst\nTuesday of the mo
 nth. We will be discussing the following\nJune 2\,\n2026\n– Looking for 
 Jane by Heather Marshall\nWe will be selecting book club titles for the f
 ollowing year.\nCopies of the book are available for borrowing at the Fair
 view Library.\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no registration necessary.
LOCATION:Fairview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6972a805d2bbe265eb294671
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d58@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nMay 9\nth\n– Dr. Strangelove
 \nMay 16\nth\n– Heaven Can Wait\nMay 23\nrd\n– Singing in the Rain\nMa
 y 30\nth\n– Green Book\nJune 6\nth\n– A River Runs Through It\nJune 13
 \nth\n– Planes\, Trains and Automobiles\nJune 20\nth\n– The Grapes of 
 Wrath (1940)\nJune 27\nth\n–\nWalk the Line\nDrop in\, no registration i
 s required.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participants. In
 gredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is in colla
 boration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d58
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
