BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beaches Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T200000
UID:696be0372c65973d001863f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively discussion about the months book pick in 
 a welcoming\, relaxed setting. New members are always welcome and encourag
 ed to join.\nJanuary 8 - The Story of Us by Catherine Hernandez\nFebruary 
 5 - Death of the Author by Nnedi Okarofor\nMarch 5 - Wuthering Heights by 
 Emily Bronte\nApril 2 - The Siren's Call by Chris Hayes\nMay 7 - That Time
  I Loved You by Carianne Leung\nJune 4 - Any Other Way: How Toronto Got Qu
 eer by John Lorinc\nJuly 2 - The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy by Dougl
 as Adams\nAugust 6 - Demon Copperhead by Barbara Kingsolver\nSeptember 3 -
  Noopiming by Leanne Betasamosake Simpson\nOctober 1 - Shadow of the Wind 
 by Carlos Ruiz Zafon\nNovember 5 - House Divided by Alex Bozikovic\nDecemb
 er 3 - The Glass Hotel by Emily St. John Mandel\nCopies of our book club p
 icks will be set aside each month at the first-floor desk at Beaches Libra
 ry. These titles are also available as eBooks and eAudiobooks through Libb
 y\, and in alternate formats.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696be0372c65973d001863f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: Newcomer Seniors' Wellness Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T123000
UID:69629af776261f280063a66a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is run by the Library Settlement Partnership (LSP
 ) and will focus on:\nLearning simple everyday English\nLearning basic com
 puter and email skills\nMaking new friends and expanding your social circl
 e\nThis program will be presented in English and Mandarin. For registrati
 on and enquiries\, please contact Wen at 647-388-3762 or email wchen@ccsca
 n.ca\nIn partnership with Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, 
 Catholic Crosscultural Services & Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Main Program Room\, First Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69629af776261f280063a66a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Microsoft Office Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260720T153000
UID:69fd0bf6caf93436005a7dae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:*PARTICIPANTS MUST HAVE MOUSE AND KEYBOARDING SKILLS*\nThese i
 ntroductory courses are for beginners. Join us in the Microsoft Office Bas
 ics series where we will learn how to work with Microsoft Word\, Excel and
  PowerPoint.\nParticipants will learn how to use basic functions including
  how to create\, save and open documents. As classes progress\, learners w
 ill build on their skills to use even more tools to design their documents
 \, spreadsheets and PowerPoint presentations.\nCourse schedule:\nJun 15th 
 : Microsoft Word 1 : Write a Letter\nJun 22nd : Microsoft Word 2 : Create 
 a Flyer\nJun 29th : Microsoft Word 3 : Craft a Resume\nJul 6th: PowerPoint
  1\nJul 13th: Excel 1 : Create a Spreadsheet\nJul 20th: Excel 2 Do more wi
 th your data
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd0bf6caf93436005a7dae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
