BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 2: Do More with your Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T153000
UID:6a05d06ee3e66a9776a98cf8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Northern District\, eLearning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a05d06ee3e66a9776a98cf8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 1: Write a Letter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T143000
UID:69ab681d8089f23c676059bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Word for absolute beginners
 .\nIn this class\, you will:\nUnderstand how to use Word’s Tabs\, Groups
 \, and Commands\nCreate\, save\, print and delete Word documents\nPractice
  basic text formatting and style features\nUpon completion of this class\,
  you will be able to use Microsoft Word at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: 
 Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations\nDrop In.
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab681d8089f23c676059bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
