BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T161500
UID:6a0217ee43b41b3d0065b7e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The North York Central Library Film Club meets monthly on Wedn
 esdays. There is a short\, informal discussion after the screening\, time 
 permitting.\nRegistration is not required. Please contact the Browsery Dep
 artment at 416-395-5672 for more information.\nThe Great Escaper (2023)\nR
 unning time: 97 minutes\nDirector: Oliver Parker\nStarring: Michael Caine 
 and Glenda Jackson\nThis film tells the true story of Bernard Jordan\, who
  made global headlines in the summer of 2014. He had staged a “great esc
 ape” from his care home to join fellow war veterans on a beach in Norman
 dy\, commemorating their fallen comrades at the D-Day Landings 70th annive
 rsary.\nNext dates:\nJuly 9 (\nThursday\n\, at 2 PM): TBA\nJuly 22 (Wednes
 day\,\nat 6 PM\n- Special Movie Night): TBA\nAugust 19 (Wednesday\, at 2 P
 M): TBA
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0217ee43b41b3d0065b7e5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
