BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Movies: My Favorite Wife (1940)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T160000
UID:6a0392428e677a28001b94c9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an afternoon of classic movies. Tea & coffee will 
 be served.\nMy Favorite Wife (1940)\nMissing for seven years and presumed 
 dead\, a woman returns home on the very day that her husband remarries.\nD
 rop-in.\nThe program will take place in the Auditorium located in the base
 ment. Elevator on site. If you have any questions\, please call Bendale Br
 anch at 416-396-8910.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Auditorium - Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0392428e677a28001b94c9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 2: Format a Flyer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T143000
UID:69ab6895491b809c6f1ea855@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Word skills and learn to use Wor
 d more effectively.\nIn this class\, you will:\nPractice new Word skills w
 hile you design a flyer\nFormat text\, margins\, indents\, headers and foo
 ters\nFormat text as columns\nCreate bulleted\, numbered and sorted lists\
 nReview your document with Spelling and Grammar check and Thesaurus\nUpon 
 completion of this class\, you will be able to use even more Word tools to
  design your documents.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1 or equivalent skill
 s. Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with dem
 onstrations\nDrop In.
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ab6895491b809c6f1ea855
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Google Docs 2: Formatting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T193000
UID:69c402148d5e2d093367860a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how Google Docs can be a useful free tool when you don't
  have access to Microsoft Word. In this follow-up class to Part 1\, use mo
 re formatting tools such as bullets\, numbered lists\, text alignment\, ma
 rgins\, page numbers\, and Help. You will also learn how to copy and paste
  text and images from the internet and explore templates for resumes and l
 etters.\nPrerequisites: Basic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFor
 mat: Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c402148d5e2d093367860a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
