BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:FULL - Seniors Digital Literacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T160000
UID:69af49d4cbf6405d3569db4c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is\nFULL.\nRichview Library will run Seniors Digi
 tal Literacy again in\nSeptember 2026\n.  If you are interested in attend
 ing the September session\,\nplease visit Richview Library to fill out an 
 application.\nSeniors Digital Literacy\nis a 6-week course designed to bui
 ld your confidence by introducing new skills slowly. At the end of the cou
 rse you will have a solid foundation of new skills and the confidence to c
 ontinue learning.\nIs This Course Right for You?\nFor seniors: beginners\,
  with very limited or no computer experience\n*6 weeks:\nwith 1 class and
  1 practice session weekly\n*This session will not meet the week of May 18
 \, 2026 due to the holiday closure.\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools suc
 h as the mouse and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, se
 rvices and entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family an
 d friends\nInternet safety\, security and privacy\nInterested participants
  must fill out an application.  Applications are available at Richview L
 ibrary.\nPlease call or visit Richview Library for additional information
 .
LOCATION:Richview\, Learning Centre\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af49d4cbf6405d3569db4c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T150000
UID:69dd0701129f127438383882@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 w​​omen and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a 
 fragility fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Os
 teoporosis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your 
 risk of osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWh
 at you need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fractu
 ring a bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical
  activity\nFall prevention
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd0701129f127438383882
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culture and Technology Book Club : Frostbite
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T200000
UID:69e6a3cfcdd2f7e31fe2bbf9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Culture and Technology Book club brings readers together o
 nce a month to discuss new and classic texts that raise important question
 s about the way technology transforms our cultural and political lives.\nT
 his meeting we'll discuss:\nFrostbite : how refrigeration changed our food
 \, our planet\, and ourselves\nNew Yorker contributor and host of the\nGas
 tropod podcas\nt explores the history of refrigeration and our changing re
 lationship to food and the notion of freshness.\nThis is a make-up event f
 or the canceled Culture and Technology bookclub meeting at Toronto Refe
 rence Library that was planned in April. All are welcome.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Elearning Lab (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e6a3cfcdd2f7e31fe2bbf9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
