BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Death Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T160000
UID:69fe7300f89ee15800518fc7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At a Death Café people\, often strangers\, gather to eat cake
 \, drink tea and discuss death. The objective is 'to increase awareness of
  death with a view to helping people make the most of their (finite) lives
 '. A Death Café is a group directed discussion of death with no agenda\,
  objectives or themes. It is a discussion group rather than a grief suppor
 t or counselling session.\nThe facilitator for this Death Café is Julie 
 McIntyre.\nDrop-in\, but space is limited.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe7300f89ee15800518fc7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
