DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T120000
UID:69ed01f5bd5c392c7646833e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is facilitated by staff in partnership with the
  Canadian Council of the Blind\, Toronto Visionaries Chapter. The book clu
 b is open to those who are living with vision loss\, low vision or are dea
 f-blind\, and to their sighted support workers\,. The book club meets on t
 he third Wednesday of every month. June's book is Grandma Gatewood's Walk:
  the Inspiring Story of the Woman Who Saved the Appalachian Trail by Ben M
 ontgomery .
