  one of the TPL Reading Challenge categories.\nThis month we will be discu
 ssing\nDaughters of the Deer\nby Danielle Daniel\nCategory Is –In Quebec
 \nIn this haunting\, groundbreaking\, historical novel\, Danielle Daniel i
 magines the lives of her ancestors in the Algonquin territories of the 160
 0s\, a story inspired by her family link to a girl murdered near Trois-Riv
 ières in the early days of French settlement.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
