BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T160000
UID:69e1448a129f12743838fdf8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nWarnings from the Ice\nScientists study air b
 ubbles in Antarctic ice cores and the movement of massive ice sheets to le
 arn how Earth’s climate has changed and what may be coming next. In a br
 ief summer window\, they brave extreme conditions to gather evidence that 
 could show how much recent warming is natural and how much is caused by hu
 man activity. Closed captions.54 minutes.1998
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e1448a129f12743838fdf8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T160000
UID:69e13d05bd5c392c7644ad93@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nWorld’s Greatest Natural Icons\nExplore wate
 r and its greatest icons\, from the Nile and Ganges to the Amazon\, Mekong
 \, and Kakadu’s vast wetlands. Witness crystal caves\, Victoria Falls\, 
 and the eerie stillness of the Dead Sea in a journey across the world’s 
 most powerful water landscapes. Closed Captions. 51 minutes. 2021
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e13d05bd5c392c7644ad93
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T160000
UID:69e13afdbd5c392c7644ad2a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nMars Calling\nSome believe Mars is the next ho
 me for Humanity. But the real “red planet” is a trickster\; strikingly
  beautiful\, yet particularly sinister. Even as a growing armada of instru
 ments arrive\, this small\, cold\, dry world conceals its secrets. This fi
 lm merges the mythic and the scientific to show that Mars may not be what 
 we imagine.50 minutes. 2021
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e13afdbd5c392c7644ad2a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
