BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fire Safety and Prevention for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T140000
UID:69fd100fc7d3cd580057bdfc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Senior Safety Awareness Month this June\, To
 ronto Fire Services will be hosting a Senior Fire Safety presentation and 
 Q&A. The topics covered include:\nPreventing a fire from happening to you\
 nCauses of home fires\nPlacement/Need for smoke & CO alarms\nEliminating n
 uisance alarms\nEscape Planning for special needs\nCalling for help (how/w
 hen/from where)\nFire safety in High-Rise buildings\nThis is a drop-in pro
 gram. No registration required.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - main floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd100fc7d3cd580057bdfc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Film Club Presents: Wicked
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T200000
UID:69fd1138703c336300262c78@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a monthly film screening of\nWicked\n(2024\, Rated
  PG).\nWicked\, the untold story of the witches of Oz\, a young woman\, mi
 sunderstood because of her unusual green skin\, who has yet to discover he
 r true power\, and Glinda\, a popular young woman\, gilded by privilege an
 d ambition\, who has yet to discover her true heart.\nDrop-in.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fd1138703c336300262c78
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
