SUMMARY:Innovation Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T200000
UID:69aeee6b45f57dfccb19679b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Conversation is the source of innovation!\nJoin TPL Innovation
  Council member\nZahra Ebrahim\nfor a series of lively book discussions ab
 out how we can build a better world by getting better at talking with eac
 h other.\nAt our June meeting\, we'll discuss the final chapters of\nTalk\
 n: The Science of Conversation and the Art of Being Ourselves\, by Alison 
 Wood Brooks. Learn about:\nLevity - how to let humour make your conversati
 ons better\nKindness - how small changes in what you say can increase war
 mth in conversation and improve your relationships\, at work and in life.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program room\, lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aeee6b45f57dfccb19679b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Online Health Information You Can Trust
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260604T150000
UID:6a0629f7703c33630027a165@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the MIRA | Dixon Hall Centre and\nDr.\nMilena Head\nfor a
  talk about finding trustworthy health information online:\nThe science b
 ehind misinformation\nHow to know what information to trust\nTips for safe
 \, confident internet use\nAgenda:\n1pm: Doors open and welcome\n1:15pm - 
 2:15 PM: Presentation\n2:15pm - 3:00pm: Discussion\, Question and Answer p
 eriod\n3:00pm: Refreshments and mingling (optional)\nAbout the speaker:\nD
 r. Milena Head\nis a Professor of Information Systems\, Wayne C. Fox Chair
  in Business Innovation and Director of the McMaster Digital Transformatio
 n Research Centre and Executive MBA program at McMaster University's DeGro
 ote School of Business. Her research focuses on digital transformation and
  human-computer interaction\, with an emphasis on how people use—and som
 etimes misuse—technology. Her work advances equity and inclusion in the 
 digital age\, exploring how marginalized groups\, including older adults\,
  engage with technology to help bridge digital divides.\nRefreshments are 
 provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the p
 rogram.\nToronto Public Library is not responsible for customer privacy re
 lated to this event's registration or evaluation.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, First Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0629f7703c33630027a165
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
