BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners: Use Windows
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T153000
UID:69dd523fb6c4ac1fedcc20fe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a 6-week course designed to build y
 our confidence by introducing new skills slowly in a small\, supportive co
 mmunity. At the end of the course\, you may not know everything about the 
 internet\, but you will have a solid foundation of new skills and the conf
 idence to continue learning.\nIs This Course Right for You?\nFor seniors a
 nd beginners\; those with very limited or no computer experience\n6 weeks\
 n: with 1 class per week\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as the mo
 use and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services and 
 entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and friends\n
 Week 1:\nUse the Mouse (May 6)\nWeek 2:\nUse the Keyboard (May 13)\nWeek 3
 :\nUse Windows (May 20)\nA class on essential basic Windows skills for abs
 olute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this session you will
 :\nBecome familiar with the Windows (10) operating system\nPractice using 
 common Windows features: File Explorer\, Desktop\, Taskbar\, Windows\, App
 lications\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic unders
 tanding of how to create and organize files in the Windows environment.\nP
 rerequisites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and keyboarding 
 skills\nWeek 4:\nUse the Internet (May 27)\nWeek 5:\nUse Google/Google Map
 s (June 3)\nWeek 6:\nUse Gmail (June 10)\nPlease read the following inform
 ation carefully:\nTo register for the\nWeek 1: Use the Mouse\nyou will nee
 d to either register\nin person at the Bloor/Gladstone Library\n\, or call
  us at\n416-393-7674\n. This first class is offline registration because n
 ot everyone knows how to use the computer mouse right away. When you are r
 egistering online\, you will be registered for all classes from Week 2 - W
 eek 6.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd523fb6c4ac1fedcc20fe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
