DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in joining a book club but are short on tim
 e?  Then join our Short Book Club\, where we read titles that are 250 page
 s or less. Meetings are held on the second Wednesday of each month.\nOur J
 une book is\nUpright Women Wanted\nby Sarah Gailey.\nSummary: “Esther is
  a stowaway. She's hidden herself away in the Librarian's book wagon in an
  attempt to escape the marriage her father has arranged for her-a marriage
  to the man who was previously engaged to her best friend. Her best friend
  who she was in love with. Her best friend who was just executed for posse
 ssion of resistance propaganda. The future American Southwest is full of b
 andits\, fascists\, and queer librarian spies on horseback trying to do th
 e right thing”\nNew members are most welcome! Please inquire at the circ
 ulation desk if you would like a copy of the book.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de5e272866a5b4884877ed
