BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Home Is Where the Identity Is: Self Expression within Historic Int
 eriors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T193000
UID:69ebac0e24bd39b0b5e86c26@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Beauport\, the Sleeper-McCann House\, the summer co
 ttage of one of America’s first professional interior designers\, Henry 
 Davis Sleeper.\nUnder the guidance of a historian\, explore the grand soci
 al spaces and intimate private rooms of this intact historic residence to 
 get to know Sleeper\, a gay man living in the early twentieth century.\nUn
 pack the floorplan and examine architectural devices in this domestic inte
 rior to discover aspects of Sleeper's identity\, ranging from his professi
 onal practice\, social engagements\, and sexuality.\nPresented by research
 er and historian Dr. Hillary Walker.\nAll are welcome. No registration nec
 essary.\nOptional registration is available for those who wish to receive 
 a reminder email or a courtesy call prior to the event.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebac0e24bd39b0b5e86c26
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
