BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memory and Aging: What's Normal\, What's Not\, and What You Can Do
  About It
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T153000
UID:69f927dec7d3cd580057008d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lecture by Psychologist Dr. Nicole Anderson as 
 she discusses the kinds of cognitive functions that change as a part of h
 ealthy aging\; and provides examples of normal memory slips\, and not so n
 ormal memory slips. This presentation discusses factors affecting cognitio
 n\, including medical factors\, and everyday lifestyle factors\, then prov
 ides a number of memory strategies that people can use to make their memor
 y function better.\nDr. Anderson is the Senior Scientist at the Rotman Res
 earch Institute (Baycrest) and  Professor\, Psychology and Psychiatry (Uni
 versity of Toronto). She is the author of\nLiving With Mild Cognitive Impa
 irment\n.\nIn partnership with CultureLink and the Active and Connected Se
 niors program.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f927dec7d3cd580057008d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
