BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hearing and memory loss: Connections\, Effects on Communication an
 d What You Can Do About It!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T160000
UID:69fe036bf89ee158005170f6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Hearing loss is a common disorder associated with ageing and i
 s associated with depression\, social isolation\, and other health problem
 s. It is helpful to know the nature of the hearing loss that most seniors 
 experience so that we can understand how it is affecting their daily lives
 .\nLearn about how to identify hearing loss\, the evidence linking it to o
 ther health conditions including dementia and brain health\, and managemen
 t options that may be available. Presented by Akram Kaymanesh\, Doctor of 
 Audiology.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe036bf89ee158005170f6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
