SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T190000
UID:69e150f54dacf581ff894287@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 w​​omen and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a 
 fragility fracture in their lifetime.\nJoin a volunteer facilitator from O
 steoporosis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your
  risk of osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nW
 hat you need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fract
 uring a bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physica
 l activity\nFall prevention\nAbout the Presenter\nThis program is delivere
 d by Osteoporosis Canada\, the only national organization serving people a
 ffected by osteoporosis. The organization works to educate\, empower and s
 upport individuals and communities on bone and muscle health and in the ri
 sk-reduction and treatment of osteoporosis with a renewed focus on reducin
 g fragility fractures.\nOsteoporosis Canada provides medically accurate in
 formation to patients\, healthcare providers and the public.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Discussion Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e150f54dacf581ff894287
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
