BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Understanding Mental Health and Well-Being in Later Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T150000
UID:69f8a59a43b41b3d0063faaa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Mental health is an important part of overall well-being\, esp
 ecially as we age. This session provides a clear and supportive introducti
 on to mental health\, mental illness\, and addiction\, and how they can af
 fect individuals in later life.\nWe’ll explore common factors that can i
 mpact mental health\, answer your questions\, and share practical ways to 
 support your well-being. You’ll also learn where to turn for support and
  resources in your community.\nThis session will be delivered by\nHope + M
 e – Mood Disorders Association of Ontario\n\, a community-based organiza
 tion dedicated to supporting individuals and families through mental healt
 h education\, resources\, and peer support.\nYour Health Matters\nThis pro
 gram is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitiativ
 e\, which offers trusted health programs and resources to help people make
  informed decisions about their health. Learn more by exploring the\nYour 
 Health Matters web page\n.\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtual event i
 s free to join but registration is required.\nPlease register on Eventbrit
 e\n.\nOnce registered\, you’ll receive an email with details on how to j
 oin the session.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f8a59a43b41b3d0063faaa
