BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Container Gardening: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spa
 ces
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
UID:69c2aa318089f23c67644b78@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing sea
 son\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not 
 choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies? This demon
 stration\, led by a Toronto Master Gardener\, will start with how to choos
 e soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize the
 ir positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, m
 aterials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.\nDrop-in\
 , no registration required.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Pl
 anet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, So
 uth Chapter.​
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c2aa318089f23c67644b78
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
