BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Traveling as an older solo woman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T150000
UID:69dff68bbd5c392c76448125@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A presentation that will leave you inspired and equipped to ex
 plore the world.\nLauraLee Giliberti is a teacher\, leader\, mother\, yogi
 \, wife and traveler. Years of traveling alone and in groups in an economi
 cal and safe way have led her to take students on tours. She’ll cover wa
 ys to explore backroads and well-known places while never falling privy to
  tourist traps.\nLauraLee is\, above all\, a student of life and is always
  observing and learning. She also believes one is never too old to live th
 eir best life.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 1st floor\, Beeton Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dff68bbd5c392c76448125
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
