SUMMARY:Senior Fire Safety Awareness with Toronto Fire Services
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T150000
UID:6a02554dc7d3cd5800588c6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of\nSenior Safety Awareness Month\n\, Toronto F
 ire Services will be presenting a fire safety presentation\, followed by Q
 &A for older adults and families. Topics covered include:\nPreventing a fi
 re from happening to you\nCauses of home fires\nPlacement/need for smoke &
  CO alarms\nEliminating nuisance alarms\nEscape planning for special needs
 \nCalling for help (how/when/from where)\nFire safety in high-rise buildin
 gs\nRegistration is required.\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Beaches\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a02554dc7d3cd5800588c6d
