BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mimico Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T120000
UID:69e24852deee9abd8ee81550@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Our book for May is The Proof of My Innocence by Jonathan Coe\
 , a political satire about Britain wrapped up in a murder mystery. Two fri
 ends uncover a sinister think-tank founded at Cambridge University in the 
 1980s that's been scheming to push the British government in a more extrem
 e direction. But speaking truth to power can be dangerous--and power will 
 stop at nothing to stay on top.\nCopies available at the library\n.\nThe P
 roof of My Innocence
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e24852deee9abd8ee81550
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
