BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Conversations with a Hakka Dragon Lady
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T153000
UID:69c402971e64afd01e64a071@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The life story of author Carol Williams-Wong whose Hakka Chine
 se ancestors worked in the sugar-cane fields and sugar factories in the Ca
 ribbean when the British contracted indentured labourers from Hong Kong to
  work in their other British colonies. Re-live Carol Williams-Wong’s hap
 py childhood in Jamaica\, eventual migration to Canada and her journey bac
 k to Jamaica.\nPlease register online or contact Hillcrest branch for assi
