BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Love hurts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T150000
UID:69ee66d01d82f930d3ca2561@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of the Love hurts movie.\nMarvin left behind a violent life to hide in sub
 urban Milwaukee as a mild-mannered realtor. He also left behind Rose\, his
  former partner in crime. Now she's back and wants Marvin to help take rev
 enge against his crime lord brother\, Knuckles. Like it or not\, Marvin fi
 nds himself back in a wild world of wisecracking hitmen with his open hous
 es erupting into warzones. He'll need his lethal fighting skills\, wit\, a
 nd heroism to survive and save the day.\nRated 14A. 1hr 23 mins.\nEnglish 
 Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ee66d01d82f930d3ca2561
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Older Adult Workshop: Lights\, Camera…It’s Never Too Late!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T120000
UID:69ef97c3c1cf6f9a7588312d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This engaging 90-minute older adult-focused workshop breaking
  down the four phases of filmmaking: pre-production\, production\, post-pr
 oduction\, and marketing/distribution. Using real-world indie success stor
 ies\, participants will learn how films are developed\, shot\, edited\, an
 d brought to audiences worldwide — proving that creativity\, strategy\, 
 and passion can turn even the smallest idea into a global project.\nNo fil
 m experience required!\nPresented by Sean Cisterna\, award-winning filmma
 ker\, pioneers filmmaking workshops for seniors 65+. He leads sessions acr
 oss Canada\, including Ontario retirement communities and festivals\, usin
 g accessible tools to spark creativity\, reduce isolation\, and build soci
 al bonds. He is the director of the new documentary\, Silver Screamers\, o
 pening at Toronto's Hot Docs Cinema on April 3\, 2026. His past films incl
 ude\nFrom the Vine\n\, Kiss and Cry\, and Full Out.\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toro
 nto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)
 \, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regi
 stration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handle
 s your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.
 ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview\, Auditorium\, Lower Level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ef97c3c1cf6f9a7588312d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
