UID:69f3ad0b762d19c7d510edaa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Cities around the world\, including Toronto\, are embracing
  the bicycle as a response to the climate crisis. This is not the first ti
 me the bicycle has come to our rescue\, proving itself a loyal friend duri
 ng times of crisis\, including the world wars and the COVID pandemic.\nIn\
 nWheeling Through Toronto\n\, author Albert Koehl takes the audience on a 
 130-year ride through the rich history of the bicycle in Toronto. By under
 standing how we got here\, we can begin mapping a way forward\, one in whi
 ch the potential of cycling is maximized.
