BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Tent on Keewatin: Building a Life in North Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T200000
UID:69f3c470fb87a3c2e2acef43@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:North Toronto Historical Society member David Penny will discu
 ss his family's humble roots in Aberdeenshire\, Scotland\, and exploratory
  trips made by his ancestors beginning in 1906 and eventual immigration to
  North Toronto in 1920. Illustrated with restored family photographs\, he 
 will cover the historical forces that led to immigration after World War I
  and how the Penny family built their first house on Keewatin Avenue. The 
 talk follows the family's life in North Toronto\, and considerable impact 
 on the community through such work as stone masonry projects\, union org
 anizing\, and public service. It is the story of one family\, but also a s
 tory that reflects how North Toronto itself was built.\nDoors open at 6:30
 pm\nPresented in collaboration with North Toronto Historical Society.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Room 200
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f3c470fb87a3c2e2acef43
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
